              text: "# MLOps Risk Assessment\n\n## Critical Risks\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Priority |\n|------|-----------|--------|----------|\n| Model drift/degradation in production | High | High | **Critical** |\n| Data pipeline failures | High | High | **Critical** |\n| Security vulnerabilities in model endpoints | Medium | High | **Critical** |\n\n---\n\n## Operational Risks\n\n### Data Management\n- **Version control gaps** → Reproducibility failures, audit trail breaks\n- **Data quality degradation** → Silent model performance decline\n- **Storage/lineage complexity** → Difficulty tracing prediction errors\n\n### Deployment\n- **CI/CD pipeline failures** → Delayed updates, manual intervention required\n- **Rollback capability gaps** → Inability to recover from bad deployments quickly\n- **Environment inconsistency** → Works in dev, fails in production\n\n### Monitoring\n- **Alert fatigue** → Real issues missed among false positives\n- **Blind spots in observability** → Undetected performance degradation\n\n---\n\n## Governance & Compliance Risks\n- Regulatory non-compliance (GDPR, AI Act)\n- Model bias going undetected at scale\n- Insufficient audit documentation\n- Unclear model ownership/accountability\n\n---\n\n## Organizational Risks\n- Skill gaps between data science and engineering teams\n- **Key person dependency** on MLOps specialists\n- Tooling fragmentation across teams\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Implement automated drift detection** with defined thresholds\n2. **Establish rollback protocols** before deployment\n3. **Define governance frameworks** early, not retroactively\n4. **Standardize tooling** to reduce fragmentation risk\n\n---\n\n*Would you like deeper analysis on any specific risk category?*",
